    <style>
      /* S5 — the HyperFrames logo outro, ported from
         projects/active/hyperframes-logo-outro/ (its README is the authority on the
         liquid-fill and flight timing). Port changes only:
           - 1920x1080 -> 1080x1080. cqw is a percentage of WIDTH, so every cqw value
             rendered at 1080/1920 = 56% of its original pixels and the outro came out
             small. All cqw sizes are multiplied by 1.7778 to restore the source's actual
             pixel sizes: mark 26 -> 46.22. The lockup is 74, not the 85.33 that rule gives: preserving
             its pixel width left only 80px of margin in a square, where the 16:9 source had
             500px. 74cqw = 799px, i.e. 140px each side. The cursor is 14.63cqw
